-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/ec2bce75-7a68-5bb3-b4c7-2aa21f001c7f
-- title:
--   Linear re-coordinatisation of a formal-group presentation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $d \in \mathbb{N}$. Let $G_v$ ($v \in \mathbb{N}$) be commutative rings carrying Hopf algebra structures over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, let $s_v \colon G_{v+1} \to G_v$ be coalgebra-and-algebra maps over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, i.e. a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each block, and the associativity identity, assumed commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $\kappa_v \colon (\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X_0,\dots,X_{d-1}]] \to G_v$ be $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra maps such that each $\kappa_v$ is surjective, $\ker \kappa_v$ is the ideal generated by the components of $\Phi$'s $p^v$-th iterate series $[p^v]_\Phi$ (defined by $[0] = 0$ and $[n+1]_i = \Phi_i([n], X)$), $s_v \circ \kappa_{v+1} = \kappa_v$, the counit of each $\kappa_v(X_i)$ vanishes, each $\kappa_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of the ideal $(p) \subseteq G_v$, each $\kappa_v$ is given by $(p)$-adic evaluation of power series at the tuple $(\kappa_v(X_i))_i$ via [`MvFormalGroup.adicEval`](def/MvFormalGroup_PointsV2.html#L20), and the comultiplication of $\kappa_v(X_i)$ equals the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $\Phi_i$ at $(\kappa_v(X_j) \otimes 1, 1 \otimes \kappa_v(X_j))_j$ in $G_v \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} G_v$. Then for every invertible matrix $P \in M_d(\mathbb{Z}/p)$ there exist a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law $\Phi'$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, a homomorphism $\ell \colon \Phi \to \Phi'$ of formal group laws whose component power series are the linear forms $\ell_i = \sum_j P_{ij} X_j$, and algebra maps $\kappa'_v$ with $\kappa'_v(F) = \kappa_v(F \circ \ell)$, such that the same nine clauses (surjectivity, kernel generated by $[p^v]_{\Phi'}$, compatibility with the $s_v$, vanishing counits, $(p)$-radicality, adic evaluation, and the comultiplication identity for $\Phi'$) hold for $(\Phi', \kappa')$, and moreover $(\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X]]/([p]_{\Phi'})$ and $(\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X]]/([p]_{\Phi})$ have the same $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dimension.
--
--   This is the change-of-coordinates (strict-isomorphism) freedom for a formal group law presenting a tower of Hopf algebras: conjugating $\Phi$ by an invertible linear substitution preserves every clause of the presentation and the height datum $\dim_{\mathbb{F}_p} \mathbb{F}_p[[X]]/([p]_\Phi)$. It is used by [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_basis_coeff_eq_normalForm`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_basis_coeff_eq_normalForm) to normalise coordinates before reading off the coefficients of the group law.
